     3	## iid uniform prices refute raw beta necessity
     4	Construction: \(P_t\stackrel{iid}{\sim}\mathrm{Unif}[0,1]\).
     5	Facts: For \(a<1\), \(\tau_t(a)\) is geometric with success probability \(1-a\), so
     6	\[
     7	\Pr(h<\tau_t(a)<\infty\mid P_{1:t})=a^h.
     8	\]
     9	Thus \(\beta(h)=\sup_{a<1}a^h=1\) for every \(h\).
    10	Why it matters: If the law is known, playing a maximizer of \(G_T(a)=\sum_{L=0}^{T-1}a(1-a^L)\) every round matches the fixed comparator in expectation, giving zero regret despite failed \(\beta\).
    11	Status: Valid counterexample to process-wise/law-aware necessity.
    12	Source: solver attempt.
